1. What is Multithreading?

Multithreading is a feature in Java that allows multiple threads to execute concurrently within a single process, helping the application perform multiple tasks efficiently.

2. What is Thread ?

Thread is a subtask of process
Thread is a lightWeight Process

By default every Process has at least one task
By default every Process has at least one thread


2 Ways to create Thread

1 : Thread class

2 : Runnable interface


******************Method 1: Thread class extend करून

class MyThread extends Thread {

    @Override
    public void run() {
        for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
            System.out.println(i);
        }
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        MyThread t1 = new MyThread();
        t1.start();
    }
}

***********interview प्रश्न: start() ऐवजी run() थेट call केल्यास काय होईल?

उत्तर: run() थेट call केल्यास तो सामान्य method call असतो; नवीन thread सुरू होत नाही.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Method	                                                                       उपयोग
start()	                                                              नवीन thread सुरू करतो
run()	                                                              thread चे काम define करतो
sleep()                                                               ठरावीक वेळ thread ला pause करतो
join()	                                                              दुसऱ्या thread चे काम संपेपर्यंत थांबतो
isAlive()	                                                          thread अजून चालू आहे का ते तपासतो
currentThread()	                                                      सध्या execute होणारा thread मिळवतो


