Q1. How many states are there in Java thread lifecycle?
Answer: Java defines six thread states: NEW, RUNNABLE, BLOCKED, WAITING, TIMED_WAITING and TERMINATED.

Q3. Can a terminated thread be restarted?
No. एका thread object वर पुन्हा start() call केल्यास IllegalThreadStateException येतो. नवीन execution साठी नवीन Thread object तयार करावा लागतो.